---Request for InvokeAgentRuntimeCommand operation.
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore.InvokeAgentRuntimeCommandRequest
---@field contentType? aws.bedrock_agentcore.MimeType The MIME type of the input data in the request payload. This tells the agent runtime how to interpret the payload data. Common values include application/json for JSON data.
---@field accept? aws.bedrock_agentcore.MimeType The desired MIME type for the response from the agent runtime command. This tells the agent runtime what format to use for the response data. Common values include application/json for JSON data.
---@field runtimeSessionId? aws.bedrock_agentcore.SessionType The unique identifier of the runtime session in which to execute the command. This session ID is used to maintain state and context across multiple command invocations.
---@field traceId? string The trace identifier for request tracking.
---@field traceParent? string The parent trace information for distributed tracing.
---@field traceState? string The trace state information for distributed tracing.
---@field baggage? string Additional context information for distributed tracing.
---@field agentRuntimeArn string The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the agent runtime on which to execute the command. This identifies the specific agent runtime environment where the command will run.
---@field qualifier? string The qualifier to use for the agent runtime. This is an endpoint name that points to a specific version. If not specified, Amazon Bedrock AgentCore uses the default endpoint of the agent runtime.
---@field accountId? string The identifier of the Amazon Web Services account for the agent runtime resource. This parameter is required when you specify an agent ID instead of the full ARN for agentRuntimeArn.
---@field body aws.bedrock_agentcore.InvokeAgentRuntimeCommandRequestBody The request body containing the command to execute and optional configuration parameters such as timeout settings.

---The request body structure for the InvokeAgentRuntimeCommand operation, containing the command to execute and optional configuration parameters.
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore.InvokeAgentRuntimeCommandRequestBody
---@field command string The shell command to execute on the agent runtime. This command is executed in the runtime environment and its output is streamed back to the caller.
---@field timeout? number The maximum duration in seconds to wait for the command to complete. If the command execution exceeds this timeout, it will be terminated. Default is 300 seconds. Minimum is 1 second. Maximum is 3600 seconds.

---Response for InvokeAgentRuntimeCommand operation.
---@class aws.bedrock_agentcore.InvokeAgentRuntimeCommandResponse
